  "full_text": "See if Mr. God is happy about that. Mr. God says, right on, good job, good job. Hope is more than dreaming. The way of the Lord is a stronghold to the upright. The righteous will never be shaken. We toss around words like faith and love all the time. Most of us can describe both with minimal difficulty, but hope, what in the world is it? And is it really essential? Webster defines hope to desire with expectation of fulfillment. Hope is to anticipate. More than dreaming, however, it is possessing within ourselves an expectation that someday there will be fulfillment of that desire. It will become a reality. Hope always looks to the future, always on tiptoes. Keep us going. Make a dismal today bearable because promise is brighter tomorrow. Without hope, something inside all of us dies. We can live several weeks without food, days without oxygen, only minutes without oxygen. Without hope, forget it.",
